	(text_box "DALI_RX is an analog signal, it is fed into the internal ADC of the microcontroller."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 123.19 118.11 0)
		(size 29.21 10.16)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1ab1d625-9725-4111-ab16-f9a65a7e1cd2")
	)
	(text_box "C17 is for noise filtering"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 182.88 135.89 0)
		(size 16.51 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "265cc8b1-aeea-4f5b-8b10-acf32e75c887")
	)
	(text_box "C6 is for EMI reduction"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 134.62 135.89 0)
		(size 16.51 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2b47370c-6969-4ae3-a420-55aa51607300")
	)
	(text_box "C15 maximum height <= 7.7mm to leave space for the vent"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 170.18 96.52 0)
		(size 34.29 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2fe75eb2-3992-4a01-a0b9-2d26a83440d6")
	)
	(text_box "This is a 2mA current limiter with approximately 1.3V dropout.\n\nD1 is for protecting the transistor against reverse base-emitter voltage when the bus is in a low state.\n\nD2 protects against backpowering. When the bus is in a low state, VBUS is pulled down by the voltage divider resistors of the DALI_RX input (see below)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 90.17 40.64 0)
		(size 43.18 25.4)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "352743c7-a96c-4b88-8558-1260dd6dfb92")
	)
	(text_box "This is needed in the self test to measure the power consumption. We pull VBUS to GND for a short amount of time, and measure dV/dt on this line."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 171.45 115.57 0)
		(size 29.21 13.97)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "39ba751a-4a18-4652-a4dc-9cdc1793e349")
	)
	(text_box "When the bus is high, we charge this buffer through the 2mA current limiter. When the bus is low (0.833ms), it powers the board.\n\nUnder normal conditions:\n  Minimum: 6.7V\n  Typical: 13.4V\n  Maximum: 19.9V\n\nD6 protects TPS62932 from >30V input."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 153.67 40.64 0)
		(size 43.18 26.67)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4c223ab3-41a8-4ee4-a721-febf2d79ef10")
	)
	(text_box "D4 is for catching smaller, low-energy voltage spikes.\n\nD5 protects against accidental 230Vac connection to the bus. In case that happens, D5 starts conducting between 25V and 40V, causing overcurrent and F1 to blow.\n\nIdle bus current: 2 mA, during transmission: 85 mA mean, 260 mA peak.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 29.21 40.64 0)
		(size 38.1 26.67)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "82f795ad-8e4b-4b2a-8288-80009506c1c4")
	)
	(text_box "R10 prevents driving the bus during bootup"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 38.1 146.05 0)
		(size 25.4 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8489d559-8eb3-41dd-b737-fb9650b924f9")
	)
	(text_box "R9-C4: filter for slope shaping"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 39.37 120.65 0)
		(size 19.05 7.62)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a3b095ec-6250-4f77-b486-b2c2bf78639f")
	)
	(text_box "A 50ms soft start is configured with the SS pin to keep the inrush current below 2mA while charging C3.\n\nThe voltage divider on the EN pin is set in a way that the device turns on above 6.6V and turns off below 5.6V.\n\nThe output is set to 2.7V because that's the minimum for the CO2 sensor. Without the CO2 sensor, we could go as low as 2.0V, which is the minimum for the analog circuitry in MSP430."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 209.55 40.64 0)
		(size 55.88 26.67)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c665c27e-e8d5-462a-b1f2-114f8914f0f8")
	)
	(text_box "This transistor needs to sink 260mA for 0.833ms, and 85 mA on average.\n\nEven though the bus is only 22.5V maximum, it should withstand 60V so the potential voltage spikes on the bus don't damage it.\n\nThe microcontroller's logic level (currently set to 2.7V) should fully turn it on with low enough drain-source resistance that it doesn't overheat.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 72.39 119.38 0)
		(size 34.29 33.02)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e6314d05-7d12-4a6b-8b3b-6ef6e3b6c624")
	)
